+  "problem": "\ud83d\udd0e **QA (BADF-QA)** \u2014 found while falsifying the central claim of #264 (`WP-UAT-B`). Not a defect in that PR; it is repo-wide and predates it.\n\n## The defect\n\n`check_schema` documents itself as *\"required keys, enum values at any depth, additionalProperties: false, string patterns\"* \u2014 and that list is exhaustive. **The walker has no `const` branch.** A `const` declaration at any depth in any schema is silently ignored.\n\nMeasured on `98747c0`, calling `check_schema` in isolation:\n\n```\nconst gate='G99'                  -> ADMITTED\nconst evidence_type='attestation' -> ADMITTED\nconst schema_version='9.9.9'      -> ADMITTED\nconst principal_type='agent'      -> ADMITTED\n```\n\n**27 `const` declarations across 21 schema files.**\n\n## Why it has not bitten yet\n\nMost consts are `evidence_type` / `gate` / `schema_version`, and those three are backstopped in code by `validate_evidence` (`scripts/badf_gate.py:1006-1010`), which pins them against the dossier and the index. So the dossier path is safe today by a redundancy nobody planned.\n\nThe exception is `uat.schema.json`'s `accepted_by.principal_type: const \"human\"`. I neutered U5's condition to `if False:` and an agent-principal `ACCEPTED` was **admitted** \u2014 U5 is the sole enforcer of that rung's central property, and the schema contributes nothing. (U5 *is* watched: the mutation fails `test_layer2_acceptance_requires_a_human_principal`. Gate restored byte-identical.)\n\n## Why it is worth fixing rather than noting\n\nA `const` that does nothing is a check that appears to guard something and doesn't \u2014 and here it actively misleads, because #264's docstring reasons *\"the recommendation vocabulary itself is closed by the schema, not here\"* four lines from a `const` where that reasoning is false. The same PR correctly removed a control (`U1`) **because** the schema really did enforce it. An author applying that correct move to U5 on the strength of the `const` would delete the enforcement and leave the appearance.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n1. `check_schema` enforces `const`: a value not equal to the declared `const` raises `ValidationError` naming the path, the declared value and the received value.\n2. A test asserts enforcement at **two depths** \u2014 a root-level const (`gate`) and a nested one (`binding.acceptance.accepted_by.principal_type`) \u2014 because the walker recurses and a root-only test would pass on a non-recursive implementation.\n3. A test asserts the **negative control**: an object whose consts all match is still admitted (the rule must not refuse conforming objects).\n4. All 27 existing `const` declarations still pass on every encoded record on `main` \u2014 run the full suite; a newly-enforced keyword can retroactively refuse landed evidence, and if it does, **that is a finding to report, not a schema to loosen**.\n5. `check_schema`'s docstring lists `const` among the keywords it enforces.\n\n**Out of scope:** any other unimplemented JSON Schema keyword. If the sweep in (4) surfaces one, it gets its own issue \u2014 this one is about `const` only.\n\n**Version tier:** patch (bug fix; no public API change).\n\nFound by mutation battery on #264, not by reading. Recommend it does **not** block #264 \u2014 the property there holds and is watched; this removes the trap under it.\n<!-- agent: reviewer -->\n",
+  "status": "AUTHORIZED",
+  "authorized_by": {
+    "principal": "operator",
+    "principal_type": "human"
+  },
+  "provenance": "EXPORTED_FROM_SOURCE",
+  "recorded_at": "2026-09-02T05:29:46Z",
+  "note": "Rung A of SARCHI's keyword ruling on #265: minLength (377 declarations across 49 files) and minItems (48 across 32). The issue's headline is `const`, which is Rung B -- the title understates the surface, as QA recorded. Plan validated by SARCHI with three conditions (failing-first + mutation discrimination as named EC7 elements; an escape case for shadowed tests with nothing to re-point at; tier reasoning plus a CHANGELOG entry). The binding gate -- re-running the zero-cost replay at current main -- was discharged before planning: 694 records, 292 refused with and without the rule, 0 newly refused."
+}
